From: pmw2-port
Subject: Make moderngekko-port usable outside the build tree

moderngekko-port resolved its source root from MODERNGEKKO_SOURCE_DIR, an
absolute path baked in at compile time. That makes a shipped binary unusable on
any machine but the builder's, and it leaks the builder's home directory into
the binary's strings - a redistributable build should carry neither.

ResolveSourceRoot() now prefers, in order:
  1. $MODERNGEKKO_SOURCE_DIR, if it points at a real tree
  2. runtime/, ., or .. beside the executable - how a bundle is laid out
  3. the compiled-in path, so existing in-tree usage is unchanged

and the compiled-in value is overridable so a release build can neutralise it:

    cmake -DMODERNGEKKO_EMBED_SOURCE_DIR=/nonexistent

Without that override the default is unchanged (CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR), so
in-tree builds behave exactly as before.

Note the path also reaches the binary through __FILE__ in assertion and logging
macros; -ffile-prefix-map handles those, but not this compile definition, which
is why it needs its own knob.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index fa2503d..2c50427 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -606,8 +613,16 @@ if(MODERNGEKKO_ENABLE_DOLPHIN_RUNTIME)
     target_link_libraries(moderngekko-port PRIVATE ModernGekko::Runtime)
     target_include_directories(moderngekko-port PRIVATE
         "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/tools")
+    # Last-resort fallback only: ResolveSourceRoot() prefers $MODERNGEKKO_SOURCE_DIR
+    # and a tree beside the executable, so a redistributable bundle never reads
+    # this. Baking an absolute build path into a shipped binary leaks the
+    # builder's home directory and is wrong on every other machine, so let a
+    # release build override it: -DMODERNGEKKO_EMBED_SOURCE_DIR=/nonexistent
+    if(NOT DEFINED MODERNGEKKO_EMBED_SOURCE_DIR)
+        set(MODERNGEKKO_EMBED_SOURCE_DIR "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}")
+    endif()
     target_compile_definitions(moderngekko-port PRIVATE
-        MODERNGEKKO_SOURCE_DIR="${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}")
+        MODERNGEKKO_SOURCE_DIR="${MODERNGEKKO_EMBED_SOURCE_DIR}")
     if(DOLRECOMP_ENABLE_LLVM)
         target_compile_definitions(moderngekko-port PRIVATE
             MODERNGEKKO_DOLRECOMP_LLVM=1)
diff --git a/tools/moderngekko_port.cpp b/tools/moderngekko_port.cpp
index af1c2a5..3abb9aa 100644
--- a/tools/moderngekko_port.cpp
